{
  "conversation_lines": [
    {
      "turn_number": 1,
      "time": "2151-06-28 13:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hello, Mr. ___. I'm Dr. ___, one of your hospital doctors. You came in today because you were short of breath, correct?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 2,
      "time": "2151-06-28 13:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, that’s right. I’ve been feeling more tired than usual, and my breathing’s been worse over the past day."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 3,
      "time": "2151-06-28 13:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I see. Your oxygen level was 88% on room air, which is low. We’ve put you on 3 liters of oxygen to help. A nasal swab came back positive for RSV — that’s respiratory syncytial virus."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 4,
      "time": "2151-06-28 13:06:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "RSV? Isn’t that something kids get?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 5,
      "time": "2151-06-28 13:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It’s more common in children, but adults with conditions like COPD or weakened immune systems — such as from multiple myeloma — can get serious infections from it too."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 6,
      "time": "2151-06-28 13:10:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Ah, I see. So that’s why I’m here. I did get my last Cytoxan dose about a week ago. I’ve felt off since then."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 7,
      "time": "2151-06-28 13:12:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, chemotherapy can lower your white blood cells and make infections like this more dangerous. Your white count is low at 2.9, and your platelets are also low — 39 — which increases bleeding risk."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 8,
      "time": "2151-06-28 13:14:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I remember — I had to get a platelet transfusion last week. And they started me on fluconazole for thrush."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 9,
      "time": "2151-06-28 13:16:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Exactly. We’ll continue the fluconazole. And because of your myeloma and low immunity, we’re giving you intravenous immunoglobulin — IVIG — to help your body fight the virus."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 10,
      "time": "2151-06-28 13:18:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "IVIG? What does that do?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 11,
      "time": "2151-06-28 13:20:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It’s antibodies from healthy donors. It gives your immune system a boost to help clear the infection faster."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 12,
      "time": "2151-06-28 13:22:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, that makes sense. Will I need it more than once?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 13,
      "time": "2151-06-28 13:24:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We plan to give it for three days. Today is the first dose."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 14,
      "time": "2151-06-28 13:26:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Alright. And what about my breathing? It’s still a little tight."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 15,
      "time": "2151-06-28 13:28:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your chest X-ray shows some patchy changes at the bases and left upper lobe — consistent with RSV. We’re continuing your inhalers: Symbicort, albuterol, and tiotropium."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 16,
      "time": "2151-06-28 13:30:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Good. I use those at home. Should I keep using the nebulizer more often?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 17,
      "time": "2151-06-28 13:32:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, we’ll have you use the albuterol nebulizer every four hours for now, even if you feel okay, to keep your airways open."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 18,
      "time": "2151-06-28 13:34:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Got it. And my Revlimid — should I keep taking that?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 19,
      "time": "2151-06-28 13:36:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "No, we’re holding both Revlimid and Bactrim for now. Your immune system is too suppressed, and we don’t want to increase infection risk further."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 20,
      "time": "2151-06-28 13:38:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay. I’ll wait to restart them until I talk to my oncologist."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 21,
      "time": "2151-06-29 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. How are you feeling today?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 22,
      "time": "2151-06-29 09:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "A little better. My breathing feels a bit easier, I think."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 23,
      "time": "2151-06-29 09:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s good. Your oxygen is now 95% on 2 liters, which is an improvement. We’ll keep the IVIG going — second dose today."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 24,
      "time": "2151-06-29 09:06:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s encouraging. I was a bit confused last night — not sure if I was dreaming or awake."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 25,
      "time": "2151-06-29 09:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, the nurse mentioned you had some moments of confusion. That can happen with infections, especially when oxygen levels are low. It should clear as you get better."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 26,
      "time": "2151-06-29 09:10:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I was worried I was losing it."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 27,
      "time": "2151-06-29 09:12:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Not at all. It’s temporary — we call it delirium, and it’s common in hospitalized patients with infections. You’re already more alert today."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 28,
      "time": "2151-06-30 10:15:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your labs this morning show your white count dipped to 1.7, but it’s expected with your recent chemo. Platelets are still low at 35."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 29,
      "time": "2151-06-30 10:17:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Is that dangerous?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 30,
      "time": "2151-06-30 10:19:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re monitoring closely. You’re not bleeding, and we avoid injections in muscles to prevent bruising. Your kidney function is stable — creatinine is 1.0, which is good."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 31,
      "time": "2151-06-30 10:21:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s a relief. My last admission was for kidney issues."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 32,
      "time": "2151-06-30 10:23:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, I saw that. But this time, your kidneys are holding up. Sodium is a bit low at 133, but we’re watching it."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 33,
      "time": "2151-07-01 09:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re on your third and final IVIG dose today. Your breathing continues to improve."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 34,
      "time": "2151-07-01 09:32:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I feel stronger. Can I start walking a bit?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 35,
      "time": "2151-07-01 09:34:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, we’ll have physical therapy see you. You’ll need help at first — we don’t want you falling."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 36,
      "time": "2151-07-01 09:36:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I did fall the other day — just tripped on my hand. No big injury."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 37,
      "time": "2151-07-01 09:38:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good you didn’t hit your head. With low platelets, even small bleeds can be risky."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 38,
      "time": "2151-07-02 10:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Lab results show your white count is up to 2.8 and platelets to 54 — that’s a good trend."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 39,
      "time": "2151-07-02 10:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Great. Does that mean I’m fighting the infection?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 40,
      "time": "2151-07-02 10:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, and your RSV is resolving. We’re stopping the azithromycin today — you’ve completed the course."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 41,
      "time": "2151-07-02 10:06:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And the fluconazole?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 42,
      "time": "2151-07-02 10:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Continue that for the full two weeks to clear the thrush."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 43,
      "time": "2151-07-03 11:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Stool and urine tests came back negative — no C. diff, no UTI. That’s good news."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 44,
      "time": "2151-07-03 11:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I haven’t had diarrhea, so that makes sense."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 45,
      "time": "2151-07-03 11:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, and your sputum was too contaminated to read, but we don’t think you have a bacterial pneumonia on top of RSV."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 46,
      "time": "2151-07-04 09:45:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re doing well. We’re planning to discharge you tomorrow."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 47,
      "time": "2151-07-04 09:47:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s great. What do I need to do at home?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 48,
      "time": "2151-07-04 09:49:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Keep using oxygen as prescribed — and please, no smoking while on oxygen. It’s a serious fire risk."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 49,
      "time": "2151-07-04 09:51:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I know, I know. But I’ve been thinking — I should quit. Can I get help?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 50,
      "time": "2151-07-04 09:53:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Absolutely. We’re starting you on a 14 mg nicotine patch daily. It can help reduce cravings."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 51,
      "time": "2151-07-04 09:55:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you. I’ve had too many lung infections."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 52,
      "time": "2151-07-04 09:57:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Smart decision. A physical therapist will visit you at home to help rebuild your strength."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 53,
      "time": "2151-07-04 09:59:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Good. I still get tired easily."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 54,
      "time": "2151-07-04 10:01:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’ll improve. Continue all your usual meds except Revlimid and Bactrim — hold those until you speak with your oncologist."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 55,
      "time": "2151-07-04 10:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And the albuterol nebulizer?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 56,
      "time": "2151-07-04 10:05:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Use it every four hours for now. If your breathing worsens, call your doctor or come back."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 57,
      "time": "2151-07-05 08:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. You’re cleared to go home today."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 58,
      "time": "2151-07-05 08:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’m ready. Thank you for taking care of me."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 59,
      "time": "2151-07-05 08:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re welcome. Remember: no smoking with oxygen, use your nebulizer, wear the nicotine patch, and follow up with your oncologist soon."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 60,
      "time": "2151-07-05 08:06:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will. And thank you for explaining everything."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 61,
      "time": "2151-07-05 08:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Of course. Take care, and we’re here if you need us."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 62,
      "time": "2151-07-05 08:10:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I appreciate that."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 63,
      "time": "2151-07-05 08:12:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your home oxygen will be set at 2 liters. The nurse will review the equipment before you leave."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 64,
      "time": "2151-07-05 08:14:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Got it. I’ll make sure my wife knows how to help."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 65,
      "time": "2151-07-05 08:16:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good idea. She can also watch for signs of trouble — like if you’re more confused, short of breath, or running a fever."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 66,
      "time": "2151-07-05 08:18:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ll tell her to call right away if anything changes."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 67,
      "time": "2151-07-05 08:20:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Perfect. You’ve made great progress. Just take it slow at home."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 68,
      "time": "2151-07-05 08:22:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will. No rushing."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 69,
      "time": "2151-07-05 08:24:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "And keep up with your catheterizations — every eight hours — to avoid bladder issues."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 70,
      "time": "2151-07-05 08:26:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, I’ve been doing that. No problems there."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 71,
      "time": "2151-07-05 08:28:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Excellent. You’re ready for discharge. The transport team will take you to your car in about an hour."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 72,
      "time": "2151-07-05 08:30:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you again, Doctor."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 73,
      "time": "2151-07-05 08:32:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re very welcome. Stay well."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 74,
      "time": "2151-07-05 08:34:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 75,
      "time": "2151-07-05 08:36:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Take care, Mr. ___."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 76,
      "time": "2151-07-05 08:38:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "You too."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 77,
      "time": "2151-07-05 08:40:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll send all your records to your primary doctor and oncologist."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 78,
      "time": "2151-07-05 08:42:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Good. I have an appointment next week."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 79,
      "time": "2151-07-05 08:44:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Perfect. They’ll help guide your next steps with treatment."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 80,
      "time": "2151-07-05 08:46:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’m glad I’m on the mend."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 81,
      "time": "2151-07-05 08:48:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "So are we. Keep up the good work."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 82,
      "time": "2151-07-05 08:50:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will. Thanks again."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 83,
      "time": "2151-07-05 08:52:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Take care. See you soon — hopefully not in the hospital!"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 84,
      "time": "2151-07-05 08:54:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Ha! I hope not!"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 85,
      "time": "2151-07-05 08:56:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Have a safe trip home."
    }
  ],
  "summary": {
    "admission_start": "2151-06-28 12:34:00",
    "admission_end": "2151-07-05 18:48:00",
    "summary_paragraph": "Mr. ___, a patient with refractory multiple myeloma, COPD, and a history of bladder cancer with neobladder, was admitted from clinic with shortness of breath and hypoxia. He had recently received Cytoxan chemotherapy and presented with fatigue and malaise. A nasal swab confirmed RSV infection, and imaging showed reticular opacities consistent with viral pneumonia. He was treated with three doses of IVIG and continued on azithromycin for community-acquired pneumonia. His respiratory status improved, and he experienced transient delirium that resolved. He was counseled on smoking cessation and started on a nicotine patch. Revlimid and Bactrim were held due to immunosuppression. He was discharged home on oxygen with physical therapy support and instructions to follow up with his oncologist.",
    "problems": [
      "Respiratory syncytial virus (RSV)",
      "Multiple myeloma, without mention of having achieved remission",
      "Peripheral stem cells replaced by transplant",
      "Atrial fibrillation",
      "Chronic airway obstruction, not elsewhere classified",
      "Hyposmolality and/or hyponatremia",
      "Hypoxemia",
      "Unspecified essential hypertension",
      "Coronary atherosclerosis of native coronary artery",
      "Personal history of malignant neoplasm of bladder",
      "Other alteration of consciousness",
      "Tobacco use disorder"
    ]
  }
}
